{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"neidhardtI","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, A→E — are each narrowed by ⅙ of the Pythagorean","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comma (≈ 698.045 cents). Four fifths — E→B, B→F♯, A♭→E♭, E♭→B♭ — are each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"narrowed by 1\/12 of the Pythagorean comma, equal to the equal-temperament fifth","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"2^(7\/12) ≈ 700.000 cents. The remaining four fifths are pure. The circle closes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly: 4×(1\/6) + 4×(1\/12) = 1 Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"From ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sectio Canonis Harmonici"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" (Königsberg, 1724). Neidhardt relabeled this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specification “Small City” in his 1732 revision.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem\/neidhardtI","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"pat